WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:06.139
"The Side Effects of Ozempic (Semaglutide)
vs. the Risks of Obesity"

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.042
Even the drug manufacturers

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:10.677
of Ozempic
and similar weight-loss drugs

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:12.246
cop to the long list

00:00:12.246 --> 00:00:14.348
of potentially serious
side effects.

00:00:14.348 --> 00:00:16.450
The absolute risks, though,

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.185
for serious issues
like pancreatitis,

00:00:18.185 --> 00:00:20.254
thyroid cancer,
bowel obstruction,

00:00:20.254 --> 00:00:22.222
were all about 1% or less

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:25.292
per year
of using GLP-1-type drugs.

00:00:25.292 --> 00:00:27.527
Of course, when millions
of people are on these drugs,

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:29.062
even relatively rare
side effects

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:31.198
will occur
in a large number of people.

00:00:31.198 --> 00:00:34.167
But you know what else
can have serious side effects?

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.802
Obesity.

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:38.472
In fact, one potential
side effect of GLP-1 drugs

00:00:38.472 --> 00:00:40.440
is that they could be
too effective,

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.342
risking excessive weight loss,

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:44.544
suppressing the appetite
so much, for example,

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:46.446
that after taking
her first dose,

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:49.116
this patient decided
to start a new diet

00:00:49.116 --> 00:00:52.653
composed of water and diet soda.

00:00:52.653 --> 00:00:56.156
Or an "eat once a week" plan.

00:00:56.156 --> 00:00:57.724
Any discussion
of risks versus benefits

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:59.426
has to take any benefits

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:03.063
of the weight loss itself
into account.

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:05.465
Excess body fat
is a major risk factor

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:07.034
for metabolic diseases,

00:01:07.034 --> 00:01:09.236
involving nearly
every organ in our body,

00:01:09.236 --> 00:01:11.171
such as Type II diabetes,

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:13.106
heart disease, stroke,
dementia, liver disease,

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:15.709
sleep apnea,
osteoarthritis, infertility,

00:01:15.709 --> 00:01:16.777
several cancers,

00:01:16.777 --> 00:01:18.211
including breast cancer
and colon cancer,

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:20.714
even psychiatric disorders.

00:01:20.714 --> 00:01:22.749
Consider
the overall health outcomes

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:24.685
of those undergoing
bariatric surgery,

00:01:24.685 --> 00:01:27.688
which is not exactly
a benign procedure.

00:01:27.688 --> 00:01:29.256
In the United States,
for instance,

00:01:29.256 --> 00:01:31.458
hundreds of thousands
go under the knife

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:32.693
to lose weight.

00:01:32.693 --> 00:01:34.261
Roux-en-Y gastric bypass

00:01:34.261 --> 00:01:36.029
is one of
the most popular techniques

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:38.398
and is thought to be
the "gold standard" method

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:40.033
given its safety record,

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:43.170
with a mortality rate
less 0.5%.

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:45.973
Wait, they’re bragging
about not killing

00:01:45.973 --> 00:01:49.209
more than 1 in 200 people
in the operating room?

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:52.079
The surgery
is a major rearrangement

00:01:52.079 --> 00:01:53.714
of your digestive tract,

00:01:53.714 --> 00:01:55.749
but it can induce
a long-term weight loss

00:01:55.749 --> 00:01:57.250
of about 25%,

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.052
which is similar
to some of the best results

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:01.021
of the new GLP-1 drugs.

00:02:01.021 --> 00:02:03.290
So, if you only care
about living longer,

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:05.125
might the benefits
of weight loss

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:08.595
outweigh the risks of dying
on the operating table?

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:11.465
Based on a meta-analysis
of millions of patients,

00:02:11.465 --> 00:02:14.167
only about 1 in 1,250 people

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:17.104
appear to be killed
directly by the surgery,

00:02:17.104 --> 00:02:18.705
and since the ones
who don’t lose their lives

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:21.008
tend to lose so much weight,

00:02:21.008 --> 00:02:22.676
bariatric surgery
has been associated

00:02:22.676 --> 00:02:25.078
with a six-year longer lifespan.

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:29.082
So, on average,
choosing to go under the knife

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:31.084
may significantly
extend your life,

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:33.086
even after taking into account
the risk

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:36.189
of the operation itself
killing you.

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:39.292
But, of course, there’s also
the risk of complications.

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:41.528
Approximately 1 in 4
bariatric surgery patients

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:43.063
experience adverse effects

00:02:43.063 --> 00:02:44.631
in the five years
following surgery,

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:46.733
and for 1 in 50,
it’s so bad

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:48.769
that they have to go back
onto the operating table

00:02:48.769 --> 00:02:50.570
for further surgery.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:53.140
That’s one advantage
of the drug approach.

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:54.674
If you experience
some serious side effect,

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:57.477
it may go away
when you stop taking the drug,

00:02:57.477 --> 00:03:00.113
whereas if you’ve already
had your stomach cut out,

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:02.015
or your intestines rearranged,

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:05.018
there may be less
that can be done about it.

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:08.155
Here’s a list
of the pros and cons.

00:03:08.155 --> 00:03:11.024
Researchers looked at
the impact of bariatric surgery

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:13.360
on more than five dozen
health outcomes.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.062
And although people
who underwent surgery

00:03:15.062 --> 00:03:16.697
may be more likely
to kill themselves,

00:03:16.697 --> 00:03:18.632
break bones,
and suffer acid reflux,

00:03:18.632 --> 00:03:22.235
they also appear
to get less diabetes,

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:23.670
high blood pressure,
and high cholesterol,

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:26.339
and less cancer
and cardiovascular disease.

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:28.408
Here’s how it breaks down.

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:29.142
Just looking at

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:32.145
the statistically
significant associations,

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:34.448
we can see that those
who’ve had bariatric surgery

00:03:34.448 --> 00:03:37.784
had a lower risk of dying
from all causes put together,

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:39.853
as well as dying
specifically from diabetes,

00:03:39.853 --> 00:03:42.089
cancer,
and cardiovascular disease,

00:03:42.089 --> 00:03:44.124
but they are
at an increased risk

00:03:44.124 --> 00:03:45.759
of taking their own lives.

00:03:45.759 --> 00:03:47.394
In terms of metabolic outcomes,

00:03:47.394 --> 00:03:49.196
lower risks of getting diabetes,

00:03:49.196 --> 00:03:50.630
high blood pressure
and high cholesterol.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:53.433
Lower risks of continuing
to have diabetes,

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:55.102
high blood pressure,
and cholesterol,

00:03:55.102 --> 00:03:57.771
and a lower risk
of diabetic complications.

00:03:57.771 --> 00:03:59.039
In terms of getting cancer,

00:03:59.039 --> 00:04:00.173
there’s a lower risk
of developing

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:01.174
different types of cancer

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:03.243
and getting
any kind of cancer at all.

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:05.512
A lower risk of all
the cardiovascular diseases

00:04:05.512 --> 00:04:07.013
the researchers looked at,

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:09.116
and most
of the digestive diseases

00:04:09.116 --> 00:04:12.018
except for reflux
with sleeve gastrectomy,

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:14.054
and higher or lower risk
of kidney stones

00:04:14.054 --> 00:04:15.322
depending on procedure,

00:04:15.322 --> 00:04:18.391
but it generally seems
to be kidney protective.

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:20.594
For women’s health,
after bariatric surgery,

00:04:20.594 --> 00:04:22.195
they had less
urinary incontinence

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:23.763
and polycystic ovary syndrome,

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:26.266
and fewer problems
during pregnancy,

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:28.201
though the outcomes
for infants are mixed,

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:30.637
with more preterm
birth and death.

00:04:30.637 --> 00:04:33.540
And finally,
less anxiety and depression,

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.008
though more self-harm,

00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:36.543
and a lower risk
of being hospitalized

00:04:36.543 --> 00:04:38.478
and dying from COVID.

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:43.183
So, generally, the benefits
far outweigh the risks,

00:04:43.183 --> 00:04:46.720
but, really, that says less
about the benefits of surgery

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:50.123
and more about the risks
of excess body fat.

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:51.224
With the GLP-1 drugs,

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:53.026
we see
largely similar improvements

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:54.127
in things like
blood sugar control,

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:55.595
blood pressure,
and cholesterol,

00:04:55.595 --> 00:04:57.664
and maybe even
similar clinical outcomes,

00:04:57.664 --> 00:04:59.132
like the risk of dying.

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:00.400
If that were the case,

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.402
then for most people
with obesity,

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:04.571
like with the bariatric surgery,

00:05:04.571 --> 00:05:06.106
the benefits of these new drugs

00:05:06.106 --> 00:05:09.009
would be expected
to far exceed the risks.

00:05:09.009 --> 00:05:11.144
Yes, there are still issues
with the cost

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:13.079
of these potentially
life-long medications,

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:15.549
and lack of knowledge
of their long-term side effects,

00:05:15.549 --> 00:05:16.616
and this, of course,

00:05:16.616 --> 00:05:19.286
assumes you’re taking
the actual drug.

00:05:19.286 --> 00:05:20.420
Shortages of these pills

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.689
have led patients
to compounding pharmacies

00:05:22.689 --> 00:05:24.991
that offer versions of the drugs
that have not been approved

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:27.027
by the U.S. Food
and Drug Administration,

00:05:27.027 --> 00:05:30.697
which in the past has led
to serious safety issues,

00:05:30.697 --> 00:05:33.233
like an epidemic
of fungal meningitis

00:05:33.233 --> 00:05:37.370
caused by moldy bottles of drugs
from compounding pharmacies.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:40.373
751 patients
were ultimately affected,

00:05:40.373 --> 00:05:43.243
and more than 60 patients died.

00:05:43.243 --> 00:05:44.778
But at least
compounding pharmacies

00:05:44.778 --> 00:05:46.780
have some kind of regulation.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:48.582
Nowadays,
people can get injected

00:05:48.582 --> 00:05:52.118
with God knows what
at so-called medical spas

00:05:52.118 --> 00:05:55.255
that may not be under
any form of regulation.

00:05:55.255 --> 00:05:57.791
People don’t seem
to be paying much attention

00:05:57.791 --> 00:06:00.727
to these FDA warnings.

00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:02.529
As an article
in Rolling Stone put it,

00:06:02.529 --> 00:06:04.531
"The FDA warned Ozempic users,"

00:06:04.531 --> 00:06:08.134
but, "They don’t give a ..."

00:06:08.134 --> 00:06:10.237
Yes, these drugs
can improve risk factors,

00:06:10.237 --> 00:06:13.039
but the risk-benefit analysis
really depends on

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:15.508
these clinical disease outcomes.

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:18.178
Do people really live longer
on these drugs?

00:06:18.178 --> 00:06:19.579
Have less heart attacks?

00:06:19.579 --> 00:06:22.816
That’s exactly
what I’ll cover, next.

